  "description": "A PARTIAL backward page, which is the path on which the page number changes not at all. PF7 from page two anchored on record six: the anchor read consumes record six, the loop reads records five down to one into screen rows ten down to six, and the sixth READPREV reports ENDFILE and sends. TRANSACT-EOF is now true, so the IF at :359 is FALSE and the entire rewind block - the extra read at :360, the NEXT-PAGE-YES test at :361, the SUBTRACT at :364 and the MOVE at :366 - is skipped. The page number therefore stays at TWO while displaying the first five records of the file, which is an inherited oddity of the program rather than a translation artefact and must be preserved (practice B5). CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST keeps its inbound value because WS-IDX never reached one; CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST is record five, written at WS-IDX ten.",
